my-cu-cli

CLI app for my-cu platform to check student information from terminal.

Tech stack:

- TypeScript
- Commander (CLI commands)
- Inquirer (interactive prompts)
- Puppeteer (automation/scraping)

Client installation (Windows, macOS, Linux)

Recommended (published package):

1. Install Node.js 20+
2. Install globally:
   npm install -g uni
3. Run the command from anywhere:
   my-cu info

Update command for clients:
npm update -g uni

Developer workflow (local source)

1. Clone repository:
   git clone https://github.com/GIORGIPUNK123/my-cu-cli
   cd my-cu-cli
2. Install dependencies:
   npm install
3. Build:
   npm run build
4. Link local CLI:
   npm link
5. Run:
   my-cu info

Release process

1. Bump version:
   npm version patch
2. Push commit and tag:
   git push --follow-tags
3. GitHub Actions workflow at .github/workflows/release.yml:
   - builds on ubuntu, macos, windows
   - publishes to npm on tags starting with v

Required repository secret

- NPM_TOKEN (npm automation token)
